marant@univ-lille1.fr (Dominique Marant) writes:

>On DEC Alpha OSF/1, is it possible that the sendmail not use DNS requests ?
>(I have hosts=local,bind in the svc.conf file)
As far as I know sendmail queries bind directly (by res_mkquery(3),
res_send(3), ...) and does _not_ use e. g. gethostbyname(3) --- at least for
some purposes like the MX records.

>All the non local mails are sending to the relay (like I want) but the system 
>do bind requests about the specified non local address (it is not necessary !).

>What are the mailer flags to specify that I want to use DNS-MX queries, or
>only DNS-A queries, or no DNS queries ?

On OSF/1 v2.0 240 (at least) the sendmail binary (5.65-IDA) is broken.
Obviously the DEC programmers forgot that their Alpha is an 64 bit machine,
where an u_long is longer than u_int.  The original sendmail-code which
extracts the answers from bind's response packet uses a sequence like
	
	/* cp points to the response packet */
	...
	ttl = _getlong(cp);
	cp += sizeof(u_long);	/* !!! */
	dlen = _getshort(cp);
	cp += sizeof(u_short);
	foo = cp;

The code gets ``out of sync'' with bind's response and the name and/or MX
query fails...

Maybe this is fixed in a later release, but I don't know.  If not, get the
sendmail source, add an q&d #define u_long u_int after all the #includes to
the file in questions (maybe it is bind.c) and recompile.

>Thanks in advance,
Hope this helps

Regards
	\franz
