In SUNOS vi, at least, when you jump to a tag  (say foo), and then from there
jump to a tag (say bar).  The tags are on a stack, so popping off the top tag
(I think it was the :po command that did this) brings you back to the tag foo.

like so:
in file x.c type :ta foo
vi switches to file y.c at line where foo is declared.
in file y.c type :ta bar
vi switches to file z.c at line where bar is delcared.
in file z.c type :po and vi switches back to file y.c where foo is declared
in file y.c type :po and vi switches back to file x.y where you started it all
