|>Whitehead) writes:
|>
|>|>My OSF/1 machine has just gone bezerk,stopping me from forking shells, 
|>|>and terminating tasks. The console is printing up message after 
|>|>message saying 'vnode table is full'.
|>|>
|>|>I have grep'd the man pages but can find no reference to a 'vnode'.
|>|>
|>|>Can anyone help.
|>|>
|>|>PS. Rebooting the system makes it go away for a week or so but then it
|>|>comes back.
|>
|>I asked someone here and they said its to do with your file system full.
|>
|>I went to our brand new OSF/1 3.0 hardcopy Docset and tried to find someting
|>analogous to the OpenVMS System Messages and Recovery Procedures manual,
|>to no avail. I have been reading the System Administration Guide and I'm
|>sure that message is mentioned somewhere, I just can't find it today. 
|>The problem is the info on error messages is not centralized but spread out 
|>in a seemingly ad-hoc fashion throughout the docs. I hope I am wrong about
|>this and some more knowledgeable person can point me somewhere useful.

We used to have the same problem here. If you look in /sys/conf/param.c,
there's a line:

#define NVNODE (NPROC + (2*MAXUSERS) + 128)

so we bumped up maxusers from the default 16 to 64, rebuilt the kernel, and
the problem has not occurred since. We're running OSF/1 2.0, if it makes
any difference.

Graham


