>Apologies if this is simple but I can't for the life of me figure out
>how you find out "simply" how much memory there is on an OSF/1 system.
> ...
>Why haven't DEC provided the tool?

getsysinfo GSI_PHYSMEM provides the hook. A little program that uses it is attached.
	-Rick
#include <stdio.h>
#include <sys/sysinfo.h>
#include <machine/hal_sysinfo.h>

main(argc, argv)
int argc;
char **argv;
{
    int memsize;

    getsysinfo(GSI_PHYSMEM, &memsize, sizeof(memsize), NULL, NULL);
    printf("This machine has %d Kb of memory\n", memsize);
    exit(0);
}

