In article <1994Oct12.180807.1@axel>,
Rebel without a Clue <foley@axel.enet.dec.com> wrote:
>In article <CxKFyu.ABI@news.cis.umn.edu>, allan@mnhep1.hep.umn.edu (Graham Allan) writes:
>
>	The RRD43 and RRD44 are Toshiba 4401 and 3401 drives. (the RRD44
>	being the more expensive/more cache drive)
>

They are oem versions that have a jumper to set the default block size
to either 512 bytes for OSF/1 or 2048 bytes for DOS.

The 4401 and 3401 are 2048 bytes/block. This can only be changed by a
scsi command.

I have got Toshiba 3301 and 3401 drives to work with OSF/1 with the
following entry in cam_data.c

/* TOSHIBA CD-ROM */
{"TOSHIBA CD-ROM", 14, DEV_RRD42, (ALL_DTYPE_RODIRECT << DTYPE_SHFT) ,
  (struct pt_info *)ccmn_rrd40_sizes, 512, DEC_MAX_REC, NO_DENS_TAB,
  &sony_mode_sel, SZ_NO_FLAGS,
  SZ_PREV_ALLOW, SZ_READY_DEF, SZ_NO_QUE, DD_REQSNS_VAL | DD_INQ_VAL,
  36, 64
},

This issues a scsi set block size to 512bytes when the device is opened.

I have tried this with an NEC 3Xp without success.

Tim.

