franck@uni-c.dk (Franck) writes:

>  I have problems with xv, or more exactly libtiff, on my APX/OSF1 box. Using the
>same xv/libtiff source and TIFF files as on my SUN/Solaries 2 I always get an error
>reading a TIFF file (something like): error in TIFF file directory count.

Get a newer libtiff from sgi.com (3.3beta2 or later will do) and change
the declarations in xvtiff.c that belong to the TIFF read/write routines
from ulong to uint. TIFF wants all ints/uints to be 32 bits long and longs 
are 64 bit on alphas.

Other programs that use the TIFF lib (ImageMagick, (net)pbm) can be made to
work in the same way.

There is still a patched version of xv with TIFF support for alphas on
ftp.informatik.uni-oldenburg.de:/pub/roleplay/xv/xv-3.1.osf1.3.tar.gz
but it want be there for much longer (till the end of the month or so).


