Tim Llewellyn wrote in article <CxxnHG.L16@info.bris.ac.uk> :
>I asked someone here and they said its to do with your file system full.

Sorry, this is incorrect.

They are data structures kept in main memory used to locate the data
blocks of a file as well as things like ownership and modification
time.  One is allocated for each file opened in the system.

Your problem can be caused by opening more files than the system
is configured for, or by programs that forget to close files.
The first problem is usually fixed by increasing the 'maxusers'
variable in the kernel configuration file and rebuilding.  The
second one is solved by fixing the buggy program.

