David McDougall (davidm@bri.hp.com) wrote:
: and I am getting a ridiculous error which states
: the following:
: "dec_interface.C:44: error: In this statement, "ioctl" is not declared."
: Now line 44 is identical in syntax to the c version and I
: have included the #include <sys/ioctl.h> line in my c++ header
: file. Does anyone know whats wrong or had a similar problem.

If you look in the ioctl.h file under OSF/1 1.3 you'll notice that there is
no prototype for ioctl in there. Fixed in (at least) OSF/1 3.0.

The error message is explicit. In C (if you didn't use -std1 -w0) ioctl would
default to an int function (which it is). If you used the -std1 -w0 option
on the C compiler it would complain abount no prototype in scope.

