In article <FARHAD.94Oct18182236@arnold.euromath.dk>, farhad@arnold.euromath.dk (Farhad Dehghani) writes:
>
>
>Is there anyone, who knows that DEC OSF/1 V.3.0, supports RZ23L disc?
>I like to install such a disc on a DEC-ALPHA 3000-500 and put the /usr
>partition on it. Is it possible? 

The supported disks for the 3000/500 in V3.0 are:

RZ24L, RZ25, RZ25L, RZ26, RZ26L, RZ28, RZ28B, RZ55, RZ56, RZ58,
RZ73, RZ74

This doesn't mean that it won't work, but it may not either.  You'll
have to try it yourself and assume the risk, if any.

As for putting /usr on one, the RZ26L is just over 100 MB.  If I
read the SPD correct, the mandatory subsets for V3.0 need 153 MB
in /usr.  All the V3.0 subsets need 303.  So you can't even fit
a minimal /usr on an RZ23L.

