>    NULL?  Seems that field is only for some special purpose.

The type field specifies the file system type.  If the CD has
a UFS file system on then you want MOUNT_UFS for the type.  If
its the ISO kind of file system, then you want MOUNT_CDFS.

The "data" structure passed is a file system specific structure
for passing the remaining arguments; one of which is almost
certainly the path name of the block special device.  In fact
if you look at the /usr/include/sys/mount.h include file you'll
see the different data structure declared (struct cdfs_args).
Unfortunately, this isn't clear from the manual page.

