  Unlike Ultrix, the OSF/1 C2 package does not automatically replace the
encrypted password fields in /etc/passwd.

  OSF/1 C2 just ignores the encrypted password field in /etc/passwd,
instead using the Protected Password Database info 'secsetup' created.

  You can replace those strings with '*' without any problem.

