>without:
>"encountering errors and possible hangs during I/O loading" as I read
>in the DEC letter?

We have about 10 RZ28B drives here with firmware below the level 
required for OSF/1 3.0. Since DEC hasn't made the correct firmware 
revision available yet, we used the kernel workaround listed in 
the release notes and have had no problems since then. The 
workaround is to disable SCSI tag queueing for the disk. You can
do this by adding the SZ_NO_TAG attribute to your disk's entry in
/sys/data/cam_data.c.

jonathan

