>In article <37bpie$8sd@nyx10.cs.du.edu>, mhatz@nyx10.cs.du.edu (Mike Hatz) writes:
>|> 
>|> Is there a script someone could send along or give a hint for a hack that
>|> displays the machine name you are logged into in the window title?

(ksh method deleted...)


I, too, log in to other systems quite a lot.

I use the following C shell (csh) alias:

alias   xcd     'cd \!* ; echo -n "^[]2;`whoami` @ `hostname`    `pwd` ^G"'

^[ is ESCAPE
^G is bell (ASCII 7)

With this, I can use `xcd' in place of `cd'. It places the
current username, hostname and directory in the window title
bar (using xterm windows).

More on this can be found in Using X by Johnson (yours truly)
and Reichard, MIS: Press.

Hope this helps,
-Eric
