Malcolm L. Carlock <malc@solstice.unr.edu> wrote:
>If started from the session manager, Xterm and DECterm fail silently --
>if xterm is started from an rlogin or telnet session into the Alpha, it
>fails at startup with a "no available pty's" message.

Have you checked the permission on /usr/bin/X11/dxterm and
/usr/bin/X11/xterm?

The permission should be '-rwsr-xr-x' and the should be owned by
root. If the 's' isn't there or they aren't owned by root they can't
allocate pty's and give this kind of messages.


