%% 
%% Is there a script someone could send along or give a hint for a hack that
%% displays the machine name you are logged into in the window title?
%% 
%% The box I am on is a DEC3000 running osf1. 
%% 
%% Thanks!
%% 
%% Mike

 Hello !!

 If you are using tcsh, change the prompt of you xterm. Add the following
 lines in your .cshrc file:

   if ( $?term ) then
     if  ( "$term" == 'xterm' ) then 
        set prompt = '%{\033]0;%m - %~\007%}%B %~ >%b '  
     else
        set prompt = '%m - %~ %# '
     endif
   else
     set prompt = '%m - %~ %# '
   endif
 
 (Note: you could add a test for testing the shell (this doesn't work under
        csh!))

 If you put this on all the .cshrc you have (I mean all machines) it will be
 nice to see the hostname and path in all your xterm (even when iconified) and
 the titlebar change when you cd in another directory. 

 Try it ! 

