Yes, I use them to set my xterm title to contain current directory and
machine. Depending on the machine I am, I use either tcsh or zsh. On tcsh, I
have:

alias precmd 'echo -n "^[]2;`pwd` ($HOST)^G"'

Where ^[ is actually <esc> and ^G is actually <bel>. This is based on the
fact, that tcsh evaluates precmd alias before it prints the prompt.

On zsh, I have

function precmd() {
	echo -n "^[]2;`pwd` ($HOST)^G"
}

since zsh uses function precmd for same efect as tcsh uses the alias.

