Dick Abraham (abrahad@govonca.gov.on.ca) wrote:
: We are trying to connect an Altek30 digitizing table to a DEC ALPHA
: 3000/400 running version OSF/1 ver 2.0b with no success.

: I have tried looking everywhere and can not find any information on
: reconfiguring the serial port for 7bit even communications.

The serial port (SCC) is a Zilog Z85C30 dual UART. It has 4 byte-width
registers at 1.E010.0000,4 and 1.E018.0000,4. Data is read/written from
byte 1 of these (accessed as longwords. Thus, by checking the Zilog spec
sheet, you can determine whether the serial port is capable of being
configured as you want (almost certainly yes). 

According to the man page, 'stty -parodd' selects even parity, and
'stty parenb' enables parity (OSF/1 v3.0). However, the situation
you describe is parity bit always 1.  You could verify that this is
true by finding at least one each of odd and even-parity bytes in
your input.  And, if so, a simple filter could convert each byte+128
to the correct value.

