Dick Abraham (abrahad@govonca.gov.on.ca) wrote:
: I can't seem to find any information on how to connect to my alpha
: running OSF/1 ver. 2 using slip protocol via a modem connection.

well...

I don't know about docs, but it isn't too difficult... I'm running slip
on a 3000/300LX with a 14.4k modem running at 38.4k DTE rate.

Its pretty simple to set up... just run the "setup" script under the root
accout and tell it you want to use slip.  If you're using dial-up, it won't
come up automatically.  Here's what we do once the box is configured for slip
via the setup script...

1. Boot the box
2. ps ax | grep sl		- Find the "slattach" process
3. kill xxx (the pid of the slattach)
4. kermit
   (dial up the service provider and log in... start the slip link on his end)
5. nohup slattach /dev/tty00 38400 &
   (this starts the slip protocol)
6. ifconfig sl0 up
7. route add default <network>
   (where <network> is the name of the network associated with the slip link)

doing a netstat -r at this point should show a sl0 link as up.

Brett Wyer


