chambles@whale.st.usm.edu (John William Chambless) writes:

>Someone pointed out in email that  Mike probably wanted a way to
>_dynamically_ change the window title, ie. have the window title
>change as he logged into a different machine.
>
>On that one, I have no clue. Anybody?

It's in the documentation that comes with xterm, but is none too easy to find.
It's in a file named ctlseqs.PS located in doc/hardcopy/xterm. It's about 2600
lines of PostScript which is why I won't include it here. It covers a lot more
than just setting the title.

The strings you are interested are near the bottom of page 4.
<esc>]0;string<bel> changes both the title and the icon to "string"
<esc>]1;string<bel> changes both the icon to "string"
<esc>]2;string<bel> changes the title to "string"
<esc>]50;font<bel> changes the font to "font"

<esc> is 33(8) and <bel> is 7.

