Daniel Garcia (kender@leviathan.ccnet.com) wrote:

: I have a program that opens the tape device, and using the mtio ioctl
: calls, controls the tape (as well as using read/write to manage data
: on the tape).  In addition to managing the placement of data, i'm also
: placing my own EOF markers.  However, as I was reading through the man
: page for mtio, it says that when i close the tape device, it deposits
: two EOF markers of it's own.  Is there any way to prevent this from 
: happeneing?

If you write your own EOF mark, and then close the device, OSF/1
will not write any EOF marks.  The only time that OSF/1 writes EOF
marks for you is if you do a write() followed immediately by close().
In that case it writes 2 EOFs to mark the end of tape.  There is no
way to prevent this.

