The above approach will work on SGI IRIX and Solaris 2.x etc. 
machines, but not on Solaris 1.

In article <373qnd$id@netserver.univ-lille1.fr>, dubus@omega.univ-lille1.fr (Georges Dubus) writes:
] On most of Unix systems the command (shell script) named "xon" can be used
] for this purpose:
] This command is provided with X11 distrib

"xon" will NOT work if the "hostname" command on your machine doesn't
give the full host name (such as that on SunOS 4.1.3), and the remote
host which you are trying to connect is outside your domain or doesn't
recognize the host name unless it's a full name...  And "xon" has only
one way of dealing with auth, which is not to deal with it -- turn
"xhost" on.

