We have also had problems reading 4mm DAT tapes produced on
SGI systems on our Alpha OSF/1 systems, also due to checksum
errors.  The following two steps work for us, so perhaps they
will work for you:

1.  Use the dd command to copy the SGI tape to a .tar file on
    the OSF/1 system.  For example:

dd if=/dev/rmt0h of=fromsgi.tar bs=512b conv=sync

2.  Then extract the resulting tar file:

tar xvf fromsgi.tar

I have heard that the problem involves the DEC system not
correctly reading the blocksize of the SGI tar tape.  Whether
the problem is on SGI's end, DEC's end, or both I do not know.

Good luck,
Michael


