Using csh the following works
setenv SHORTNAME `hostname | cut -f1 -d.`
echo -n "^[]2;$SHORTNAME

Actually, I have the working directory displayed too - simple addition
to the above
setenv SHORTNAME `hostname | cut -f1 -d.`
alias cd 'cd \!*; echo -n "^[]2;$SHORTNAME : `pwd`^G"'

Using the fancier perl script "prunepwd" you can "prune" the directory 
name too ...

