In article <37bpie$8sd@nyx10.cs.du.edu>, mhatz@nyx10.cs.du.edu (Mike Hatz) writes:
|> 
|> Is there a script someone could send along or give a hint for a hack that
|> displays the machine name you are logged into in the window title?
|> 
|> The box I am on is a DEC3000 running osf1. 
|> 
|> Thanks!
|> 
|> Mike

This is bash/ksh:

newcd()
{
        \cd $*
        PS1="$PWD>"
        if [ "$TERM" = "xterm" ] ; 
        then
          wintitle="`hostname`:$PWD    [`ls -ld . | awk '{print $1,$3,$4}'`]" 
          icntitle=`hostname`:...`basename $PWD`
          echo -ne "\033]2;$wintitle\007"
          echo -ne "\033]1;$icntitle\007"
         fi

}

alias cd newcd

