In article <1994Oct4.154244.714@zeno.mscd.edu>, labelles@zeno.mscd.edu (Stephen LaBelle - MSCD) writes:
> I am curious if it is possible to put on OSF/1 system on Bitnet? 
> 
> I have heard of development/porting of NJE to unix systems.
> 
> Can anyone help or point me in the right direction?

  A few responses have shown where to get VMS software for NJE, but didn't
give any resources for Unix versions. As far as I know, neither Jnet nor
ANJE come in a Unix version.

  The two packages I *do* know about are UREP and Huji-NJE. UREP is from
PSU (where Jnet was originally developed). You can get more info from
ftp.cren.net in the file /pub/bitnet/bitnet-doc/urep.info. I've never tried
to run UREP - there is a hefty license fee and the software is widely re-
garded on BITNET as buggy. Huji-NJE is free (or was when I got it), and
works reasonably well. You can get info from the same FTP server as above,
except the filename is huji-nje.info.

  Neither of these is as full-featured as Jnet on VMS (or RSCS on VM), but
they may be enough for you. They'd at least be a starting point if you wanted
to add some enhancements.

