I've used xmgr on our HP9000 machine, and I thought that it was fine
for quick and dirty graphs, but creating pretty graphs was a very
long process. The editing tools will mostly take an atomistic approach
to what you are editing, and simple tasks - like changing the font to 
Times - can require a great deal of navigating. The PCL drivers were 
more of a liability than an asset.

IMHO the best solution for making truly pretty figures is to use any
program that'll create a metafile output (or HPGL if this is not 
feasible) for drawing the basic graph, and then insert all the numbers
on the axises, titles, little boxes etc. in CorelDRAW or some similar 
program. It's not the fastest method for a fast graph, but if you need
to do a lot of detailed adjusting it is far and away the best.




Thomas





