Hi everybody!

I have some questions about printing from OSF/1.

We have some Alphas with OSF/1 (I hope in the near future all with
Version 2.1), some other Unix machines and an VMS-cluster.  Our
printers (all Postscript) are distributed over several buildings and
usually attached to the LAN (Ethernet) via terminal servers. Up to now
the print requests are handled by the VMS-cluster using the UCX-LPD,
but this becomes more and more a bottleneck. On the other hand, we
decided for management reasons, that print requests should be handled
by very few central nodes.

Does anybody knows about software that recognizes the datatype to
print (Postscript or ASCII), that converts ASCII automatically to
Postscript and that prepares nice flagpages? Maybe a modified version
of 'a2ps'?

Let's assume we have established such an Alpha that handles print jobs
for printer PRINTER. From an other machine PRINTER is reachable over
two ways: via the Alpha and via the VMS-cluster. How can I setup
PRINTER on this other machine to reach PRINTER via the Alpha as a
default route and (if it is down) to direct the data to the
VMS-cluster? 
One idea is to establish execution printers PRINTER_ALPHA and PRINTER_VMS
and a generic printer PRINTER. The latter one could use a shellscipt as
input filter like:
if 'lpq -PPRINTER_ALPHA' is ok? then
	lpr -PPPRINTER_ALPHA -
else if 'lpq -PPRINTER_VMS' is ok? then
	lpr -PPRINTER_VMS -
else
	echo blabla
end if
Are there any other more convinient solutions/suggestions?

I do not read this newsgroup regularly, please e-mail your ideas to
gnolte@msfd12.gwdg.de. I'll post a summary of your reactions to the newsgroup.

