>get the lmgrd daemon to startup at boot, we put the command in /sbin/rc3.d
>at the end, as something like S96lmgrdstart. In the file we put the
>command "{path}/lmgrd -c {path}/license.file" followed by an "&" to keep 
>the boot going. No dice. No errors messages. Changing the command to 
>"sh {command} &" did nothing for us either. We finally gave up and 
>hardwired it into the end of rc3 itself with no &, whereapon it works, and
>xdm comes up. This is not ideal as it still has the console, but it doesn't 
>seem to want to do anything when started in the background. I never 
>encounter this problem with any other version of unix and rc files. When 
>started on the command line by root, lmgrd runs fine in the background.

We use several packages that implement FlexLM. My lmgrd comes from LSF and 
starts roughly like this:

$LSF_SERVERDIR/lmgrd \
	-c /usr/lsf/etc/license.dat | sh -c \
	'while read line; do echo "$line" >> /var/adm/flexlm.log ; done ' \
	2>&1 &

I have this by itself in /sbin/init.d, with a link from /sbin/rc3.d 
pointing to it. It isn't very elegant if you ask me, but then again, I
haven't had any problems with it here.

jonathan

