And to answer the other questions: yes other people use it too.
(Sun since SunOS 4.x).  And no, there is no more accurate method.

If the rules change, edit the rule file and recompile.

The timezone directory is the actual source of the timezone/timechange info.
However, you should understand that tehre is no such thing as a "timechange"
from teh OS'es point of view: the OS clock ticks in seconds since
"0:00 Jan 1 1970 GMT".  Whenever you ask the time, this is converted
using the timezone data to your local time.  When daylight savings
time ends, a different conversion rules becomes applicable.  The
clocks seems to jump an hour, but until you look nothing notices.

Casper



