In article <36p9hq$h2u@wave.aoml.erl.gov>, chen@news.aoml.erl.gov (Ying-Yuang Chen) writes:

>	I just got a Seagate ST15150N 4GB disk for my alpha OSF1. Does 
>anyone have the disktab entry for this drive or is there any other way to 
>format and partition it?

The disklabel command get the geometry information from the drive
itself and will use a default partitiont table.  Once a label has
been written, it can also be edited to modify the partition table
to taste.  You may also want to set the correct rotational speed
since disklabel can't get it from the driver.

Example:

# disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c st15150n

If it can't find the disk type in /etc/disktab, then it just
asks the driver for the information.

>	BTW, what is the max. size for OSF1 file system ?

The V2.0 SPD has the file system size limit listed as 32 GB.  I
suspect this is a limit based on what was tested.  According
to the V3.0 SPD, the UFS file system size limit is still 32 GB,
but the Advanced File System has a limit of at least 128 GB
(largest supported file).  The real limit are probably up in
the TB range.

