From: Kjell Randa <bg53079@bginu6.nho.hydro.com>
We have been using Flexlm on Alpha for both AVS and BuildeXccesory for quite
some time without problems. For AVS we have the following setup:
 
In /sbin/init.d we have a file named flex containing the following:
 
#!/bin/sh -f
# Start/stopp av Flex.  18/8 94 Kjell Randa
#
USAGE="Usage: $0 start|stop"
if [ $# != 1 ];then
   echo $USAGE
   exit 1
fi
if [ -f /etc/lmgrd ];then
case $1 in
        'start')
           /etc/lmgrd -c /usr/avs/license/license.dat > /var/flex/flex.log &
           echo "Flex licence manager started"
           ;;
        'stop')
           /etc/lmdown -c /usr/avs/license/license.dat -q
           ;;
        *)
           echo $USAGE
           exit 1
esac
else
        echo 'No Flex installation found, exiting'
        exit 1
fi
 
In /sbin/rc3.d we have a file named S90flex which is a link to the flex file
listed above.
 
In /sbin/rc0.d we have a file named K17flex which is also a link to the above fle.
 
This start and stop the Flexlm licence manager at system startup and shutdown.
 
Tu use avs with this setup each user has to issue the following command prior tstarting avs:
 
setenv LM_LICENSE_FILE /usr/avs/license/license.dat
 
Regards
Kjell Randa
Norsk Hydro
NORWAY
 


