Your lmgrd is probably getting killed by the getty revoking the terminal
from previous sessions.
 
Try a wrapper around the lmgrd like this:
 
detach lmgrd <args>
--mysteryboxofun
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=US-ASCII; name="detach.c"
Content-Description: ~/src/detach.c
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
 
main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    close(0);
    close(1);
    close(2);
    setsid();
    ++argv;
    execv(argv[0], argv);
}
 
 
--mysteryboxofun--


From: boccio@cc.swarthmore.edu (John Boccio)
 Hi,
 
I use the license manager from AVS. It is used by AVS, MATLAB and IDL.
 
The following file is in /sbin/rc3.d
 
It is name S67lmgrd
 
The number 67 just makes it start after lpd.
 
We have had now trouble at all.
 
John Boccio
boccio@cc.swarthmore.edu
 
# Control the Flexlm license manager daemon
#
 
PATH=/sbin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin
export PATH
 
AVS_PATH=/usr/local/avs
LM_LICENSE_FILE=/usr/local/avs/license/license.dat
export AVS_PATH LM_LICENSE_FILE
if [ -x ${AVS_PATH:-/usr/avs}/license/lmgrd ]; then
  echo Starting lmgrd
  ${AVS_PATH:-/usr/avs}/license/lmgrd \
  -c ${LM_LICENSE_FILE:-/usr/local/flexlm/licenses/license.dat} \
  -l /tmp/lmgrd.log -2 -p &
  sleep 5
fi
 

From: Irving Reid <irving@sys.toronto.edu>
Did you redirect the output from lmgrd somewhere?  lmgrd normally writes
its log messages to standard output, and that might be biting you.
 
I work for a company that distributes a package that uses FLEXlm on OSF/1,
and we haven't had any problems like yours.
 
If you don't mind having all your FLEXlm messages in the syslog log, try
 
{path}/lmgrd -c {path}/license.dat | logger -t lmgrd -p local2,info 2>&1
 
