In article <3686o3$sqf@pellew.ntu.edu.au>, dmoon@obiri.ncom.nt.gov.au writes:
>We are running osf1 version 1.3 on a Dec Alpha system.
>
>How do we set passwords to automatically expire after 30 days?
>
>I'm sure I've read somewhere how to do it.
>
>(Suns use passwd -x, but this is not a feature of osf1.)
>

  Password expiration is a feature of the C2 Enhanced Security option
included with the normal distribution of OSF/1 starting with version 2.0.
Make sure that you have loaded subset OSFC2SEC2xx; where xx is the
version info. Information on the enhanced security version of the
'passwd' utility is contained in the man page. Further information on
configuring C2 security, and on ISSO administration of password options
can be found in the DEC OSF/1 Enhanced Security manual, included either
with your printed doc set (if ordered) or with the CDROM online docs
included with the OSF/1 >v2.0 binaries distribution.
 
