I had a similar problem. We have many Macs on the net. For interfacing the
ethernet, they use a so-called 'friendly-net' adapter. It has two BNC plugs;
normally, you use both of them (one in, one out). If you leave one of them
open, a switch is activated which terminates the line automatically. So what
happened was that they used EDA cables, which only have one plug. That way
we had about five terminators in the line, messing up everything. Before we
got the DEC 3000, nobody had noticed that, because the Macs are so slow
anyway. After I had put empty plugs on the adapters, everything was fine.

I don't think it has anything to do with the Alpha station.

Hope I could help.

