First, you're right -- dump under OSF/1 is extremely sensitive and 
multi-user mode dumps (in my experience) result in tons of unrecoverable
files on the tape.  We never had trouble on that scale with the Suns.

Second, the best way to index a dump archive, in my opinion, is to just
write the index to a file on the root directory of the partition you're
backing up before you back it up.  Time stamp it in the filename for
easy identification during an interactive restore.

>3)  The use of tar is out because it requires all of the file names to
