>    including files on a different file system if that mount point is
>    included in any directory being backed up.

I think you're wrong about this not being an option.  Have you tried
using the "-I" include file syntax?  If OSF/1 doesn't support it (not
sure offhand) then I'm sure GNU tar will, and GNU tar will handle 
special devices too.

>Short of taking the Ultrix source we have for cpio and porting it to
>OSF/1, I am out of ideas.

